.TH SDL_MALLOC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_MALLOC \- A macro to tag a function as an allocator.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_MALLOC __declspec(allocator) __desclspec(restrict)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a hint to the compiler that a function is an allocator, like malloc(), with certain rules\[char46] A description of how GCC treats this hint is here:
.PP
https://gcc\[char46]gnu\[char46]org/onlinedocs/gcc/Common-Function-Attributes\[char46]html#index-malloc-function-attribute
.PP
On compilers without allocator tag support, this is defined to nothing\[char46]
.PP
Most apps don\(aqt need to, and should not, use this directly\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

